Run these two

D1: Names of the APMIDs C2 flagged (problems with exactly one APMID, so the name pairing is unambiguous)

fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-7d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter dt.davis.is_duplicate == false
| filter not(contains(lower(toString(entity_tags)), "portfolio:claims"))
| expand tag = entity_tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:") or startsWith(tag, "APPName:")
| fieldsAdd apmid   = if(startsWith(tag, "APMID:"),   splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]),
            appName = if(startsWith(tag, "APPName:"), splitString(tag, "APPName:")[1])
| summarize apmids = collectDistinct(apmid), names = collectDistinct(appName), by:{display_id}
| filter arraySize(apmids) == 1
| fieldsAdd apmid = apmids[0]
| summarize problems = count(), appName = takeAny(names), by:{apmid}
| sort problems desc
| limit 50


This shows which of the flagged apps are Claims and which are platforms. If collectDistinct keeps nulls or takeAny errors, send me the error and I'll adjust it.

D2: Claims container apps (APMIDs from namespaces)

fetch dt.entity.cloud_application_namespace
| fields id, name = entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "portfolio:claims")
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| summarize namespaces = countDistinctExact(id), nsNames = collectDistinct(name), by:{apmid}
| sort namespaces desc


I expect the APP00236xxx apps here. Any APMID in this list is a Claims app, whether or not it shows up on Claims hosts.

